"""Japanese-romanisation passages (isekai / shonen / school register). Original prose."""

PASSAGES = [
("ja01", """[[Satoru Gojo|p]] was late again. The students of [[Kuroi Academy|o]] had stopped counting. “[[Gojo-sensei|p|tit]] is here!” someone shouted, and the class scrambled. In the staff room the principal, whom the older teachers called [[Gojo Satoru|p]] only when they were angry, sighed. “Which [[Gojo|p]]?” asked the substitute. “There are two on the register.” He pointed at the strongest sorcerer in the building, also known as [[the Honoured One|t|ali]], and then at a quiet history teacher with the same family name, [[Gojo Mari|p]]."""),
("ja02", """“[[Rain-chan|p|tit]]! Come inside!” cried the housekeeper. [[Rain|p|wl]] pulled her hood down and walked on through the market of [[Hoshizora Town|l]]. She was a witch, though no one knew it, and her master was [[Lord Aizen|p|tit]], an old magician. “[[Rain-chan|p|tit]],” he had said, “the [[Moon Pearl|i]] must reach the [[Order of the Silver Owl|o]] by dusk.” On the way she met [[Takeda-san|p|tit]], the baker, who handed her a warm roll. “Thank you, [[Takeda-san|p|tit]].” “Mind the rain,” he said, laughing."""),
("ja03", """[[Haruto|p]] woke in an unfamiliar bed. A girl with silver hair bowed. “[[Haruto-sama|p|tit]], the [[Demon King|t|ali]] awaits.” “Who?” “[[His Majesty|t|ali]].” Everyone in the castle of [[Shirogane|l]] used these three expressions for one man, whose true name, [[Zenobel Karst|p|inv]], was never spoken. [[Haruto Kisaragi|p]] sat up slowly. The sword by his bed was [[Dawn Cleaver|i]]. He had no idea how it got there, nor why the [[Adventurers' Guild|o]] was waiting downstairs."""),
("ja04", """[[Tanaka-kun|p|tit]] was the class representative of 2-B. [[Tanaka Ren|p]] never said much. Another [[Tanaka|p]], [[Tanaka Mio|p]], sat in 2-A, and the two were constantly confused. “Which [[Tanaka|p]] broke the window?” the teacher asked. “[[Mio-chan|p|tit]],” said a voice. “No, [[Ren|p]],” said another. At the other end of the hall stood the [[student council president|t]], holding a clipboard and refusing to take sides. Behind him, the sign of [[Aoba High|o]] glowed in the afternoon sun."""),
("ja05", """The [[clan head|t|sh]] of the [[Kurosawa clan|o]] and the [[clan head|t|sh]] of the [[Shinjo clan|o]] were cousins, and so both were called [[uncle|t|sh]] by half the district. “[[Uncle|t|sh|gen]] has refused,” reported [[Kurosawa Jin|p]]. “Which one?” “Mine.” The two houses had fought over the river since before [[Lord Oda|p|tit]] unified the province. Their ancestral blades, [[Thunder Crane|i]] and [[Morning Heron|i]], hung unused in their halls. In [[Edo|l]], the shogun's envoy waited for answers."""),
("ja06", """Hope? There was none, said [[Hope|p|wl]], the stray cat, to nobody. [[Nozomi|p]], which means the same thing, scratched her ear. “[[Nozomi-san|p|tit]], breakfast.” “I'm coming.” Beyond the garden wall lay [[Sakura Ward|l]], full of people who believed in luck. [[Nozomi|p|si]] did not. She worked at the [[Lantern Bookshop|o]] and wrote letters for the elderly. A man in a grey coat, called [[Sensei|t|ali]] by the neighbours, visited every Friday and paid in oranges."""),
("ja07", """[[Isekai Hunter|t|ali]] was the title printed on [[Kaito|p]]'s guild card. In the [[Guild of Seven Banners|o]] he was only [[Kaito-san|p|tit]]; in the tavern he was [[Kai|p]]. “[[Kai|p]]!” called the barmaid. “[[Sir Kaito|p|tit]],” corrected a knight. The city of [[Elmira|l]] knew him as one man with three names. In his pack lay the [[Starfall Compass|i]], bright with unused magic. Outside, the [[city lord|t]] was raising a toast to the heroes, and not one of them had asked [[Kaito|p]]."""),
("ja08", """[[Yui|p]] and [[Yuri|p]] looked alike but were not related. At [[Seiran Girls' School|o]], people mistook one for the other. “[[Yui-senpai|p|tit]]!” cried a first-year. “Wrong one,” said [[Yuri|p]]. “[[Yuri-senpai|p|tit]]!” “Better.” In the library, [[Librarian Morita|p|tit]] stamped returns. Heaven help the student who returned a book late. The old woman had a ledger and a memory like a trap. On the roof the two girls ate lunch beneath a sky the colour of milk, safe from the [[Discipline Committee|o]]."""),
("ja09", """[[Mizuki|p]] ran. Behind her, the [[Shadow Court|o]] howled. Sentence by sentence her breath grew shorter; the corridors of [[Ryuuzen Castle|l]] twisted. She remembered her mother's advice: do not look back. At the great hall waited the [[shrine maiden|t]], the one whom the villagers revered as [[Miko-sama|p|tit]] and whom the court clerks recorded as [[Lady Hinako|p|tit]]. [[Hinako|p|si]] smiled. “[[Mizuki-chan|p|tit]], you came.” In her hands lay the [[Mirror of Nine Clouds|i]], cold and bright."""),
("ja10", """[[Ichigo|p|si]] was also a fruit, and everyone made the joke. [[Ichigo Aoyama|p]] ignored them. At the dojo of [[Bright Pine|o]], the master, [[Master Sato|p|tit]], called him [[Aoyama-kun|p|tit]] while the older boys called him [[Strawberry|p|ali]]. All three names meant the same sullen boy, who held a bamboo sword like a weapon. “Again,” said [[Sato-sensei|p|tit]]. Dust rose from the floor. Outside the gate of [[Nagano|l]], snow began to fall."""),
("ja11", """Nothing was left of [[Black Rose Manor|l]] but chimneys. [[Lord Ashikaga|p|tit]] walked through the ash, with his retainer [[Kenji|p]] a step behind. “[[Ashikaga-sama|p|tit]], the [[Imperial Court|o]] sent no word.” “It will.” The two never spoke of the fire. “[[Kenji|p]], bring the [[Iron Fan|i]].” “Yes, [[my lord|t|ali]].” Whoever had set the fire had left a single paper crane on the doorstep, folded in the style of the [[Hidden Leaf Order|o]]."""),
("ja12", """[[Aiko|p]], [[Akio|p]], and [[Akira|p]] ran the shop together. Customers constantly mixed up the three. “[[Aiko-san|p|tit]], two buns!” “I'm [[Akio|p]],” grumbled the man at the counter. The shop was called [[Three Pines|o]], and it sat in the lane behind [[Tsukimi Station|l]]. Their landlord, the old man who owned half the street and was known to the neighbours as [[Landlord Mori|p|tit]], collected rent every month. “Tell [[Akira|p]] he owes me tea,” he muttered."""),
("ja13", """“[[Tsubasa|p]], wake up.” [[Tsubasa Arai|p]] groaned. The morning sun lit the room of the dormitory at [[Fujimori Academy|o]]. Heaven, he thought, was a long weekend. “[[Arai-kun|p|tit]], assembly!” His roommate, [[Sota|p]], tossed him a tie. In the hallway, the [[vice-principal|t]] was already collecting late students. “[[Sota-kun|p|tit]],” she said, “you too.” Neither noticed the strange letter sealed with the mark of [[the Crimson Moon|o|ali]]."""),
("ja14", """In village [[Hanabi|l]], two elders kept the shrine. [[Elder Tsuda|p|tit]], the tall one, and another [[Elder Tsuda|p|tit]], the small one, were unrelated and bore the same surname by accident of history. “[[Tsuda-sama|p|tit]],” said the pilgrim, bowing, “which of you holds the [[Heron Scroll|i]]?” “Neither,” said both. The shrine guardian, a fox spirit known as [[Inari-sama|p|tit]], yawned in her sleep. Wind rattled the [[Gate of Ten Thousand Lanterns|l]]."""),
("ja15", """The student known as [[Yamato|p]] never gave his surname, so some wrote [[Yamato Kuze|p]] and others [[Kuze Yamato|p]]. Both were him. In [[Kyoto|l]], where he lived, they said [[Kuze-san|p|tit]]; online, he was [[Night Hawk|p|ali]]. “[[Yamato|p]], the [[Seventh Division|o]] called,” said [[Captain Reiji|p|tit]]. “They want you.” “For what?” “For the sword.” He touched [[Kusanagi's Shadow|i]] and thought of home. Rain began to fall on the roofs of the old city."""),
]
